node_modules/
.env
*.log
.DS_Store
server/.DS_Store
.vercel/
.vercel

# Client-supplied brief documents. Kept local: they carry RS's company details
# and a named contact, which should not sit in a repository that could become
# public. The requirements themselves are reflected in report/CLIENT_ANSWERS.md
# and the report, which are written for sharing.
/Requirements
/Questionary-Requirement
*.pdf

# Runtime state, not source. Daily snapshots are what make day-over-day deltas
# possible; they are regenerated on every refresh. Point SNAPSHOT_DIR at a
# mounted volume in production so history survives redeploys.
data/snapshots/

# NOTE: server/public/vendor/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Chart.js is
# committed so the dashboard renders on an egress-restricted internal network
# with no CDN access. `npm run vendor` refreshes it from node_modules.
